# Checkmate in Time Line Fragment (4x4, two timelines), found with a search over the engine: White steps the king
# (a1 -> a2) on the white-moveable board, then Black plays pawn b4-b3 on the first board and bishop b4-a3 on the
# second; White then has no legal turn and its king is attacked: "Black wins!" (Checkmate).
# Layout (1400x800): Versus (150,280); mode row 8 (690,634); Play (808,712). Boards are 252 px (63.3 px squares, files
# a..h from the left): the white-moveable one at x 415..667, y 466..718; after white submits, black's boards sit at
# x 732..985 (y 149..402 and y 466..718).
wait 20
click 150 280        # Versus
wait 30
click 690 634        # Misc - Time Line Fragment (row 8)
wait 20
click 808 712        # Play
wait 120
capture endgame-start
click 636 687        # white king (bottom-left board)
wait 40
click 636 623        # one step up
wait 40
click 841 90         # Submit
wait 90
capture endgame-black-to-move
click 890 181        # black pawn on the top board
wait 40
click 890 244        # one step down
wait 60
capture endgame-black-first-move
click 731 498        # black bishop (bottom board: the view re-centred after the first move)
wait 40
click 795 561        # diagonal step
wait 90
capture endgame-black-second-move
click 841 90         # Submit: White has no legal turn
wait 150
capture endgame-end-card
